Third-Party Data Sources (Public Domain or Government Works)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

U.S. Environmental Protection Agency - Enforcement and Compliance History
Online (ECHO). Facility data used in scripts/verify_facilities.py and
facilities.json. U.S. public domain / government work.
https://echo.epa.gov/

U.S. Environmental Protection Agency - EJScreen Environmental Justice
Screening and Mapping Tool. Block-group environmental and demographic
indicators used in scripts/update_ejscreen.py,
scripts/fetch_ejscreen_history.py, scripts/seed_history_from_baseline.py,
de_blockgroups.geojson, and de_blockgroups_history.json. U.S. public domain /
government work.
https://www.epa.gov/ejscreen

U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention - PLACES: Local Data for
Better Health. Census-tract health estimates used in
scripts/build_places_tracts.py and places_tracts.json. U.S. public domain /
government work.
https://www.cdc.gov/places/

U.S. Census Bureau - TIGER/Line Shapefiles. Block-group and tract boundary
geometries. U.S. public domain / government work.
https://www.census.gov/geographies/mapping-files.html

Delaware Sea Level Rise Technical Committee - 2017 Sea Level Rise projections
(1/3/5/7 ft scenarios). Data files in climate/ directory. Government work;
attribution requested.
https://dnrec.delaware.gov/climate-coastal-energy/climate-change/slr/

